Package: Rjif
Title: The 'Jif' Statement: Judgment-Based Control Flow via TypeSafe Jev
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yue", "Shentu", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "n43368410@gmail.com")
Description: Replaces hard-coded 'if' conditions with semantic decisions
    gated by explicit abstention. Wraps the TypeSafe Jev 'System One' API
    (Choice, Score and Noul primitives) and provides jif()/jmatch()
    control-flow verbs plus a vectorized evaluator that scores whole vectors
    of narratives (for example eCRF adverse-event text) one state per API
    call, with confidence floors, abstention sentinels and selection-failure
    analytics for auditing reliability. Calibration is measured, not
    asserted; see the reliability diagnostics.
